<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank sets tender for 16-day repos at 3 pct.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank sets tender for 16-day repos at 3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Tuesday it was setting a tender for 16-day securities repurchase funds, offering banks liquidity at a fixed rate of 3.00 percent.</p>
<p>Funds will be credited to accounts tomorrow and the securities have to be repurchased on December 27.</p>
<p>A 69.7 billion mark facility will expire on Wednesday. The repo rates has been fixed at 3.00 percent since late August.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
